# Keep the image to the product and its corpus.
#
# corpus/ and .sanhita/ are deliberately NOT ignored here even though git
# ignores them. The container needs the circular and the compiled rulebook, or
# it boots to an empty screen.

.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
tests/
eval/
data/
themes/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.md

# Uploaded workspaces are one person's documents on one machine. They must not
# be copied into an image that other people will open.
.sanhita/workspaces/
.sanhita/users.json

# Per-visitor copies of a firm's own data, on a shared deployment. These are
# named `company.u<id>.json` and so on, keyed to an account id from *this*
# machine. The image builds its own accounts, so those ids match nobody in it:
# copying them in ships an orphan carrying one developer's demonstration state
# that no visitor can ever reach. `demo-seed` writes the correct ones during
# the build, scoped to the officer it creates there.
.sanhita/*.*.json

# Most of the other circulars are for local testing of the upload path.
# Shipping all seven would add 20 MB for no benefit to a first-time visitor.
#
# The two Investment Adviser editions are the exception and they are worth
# their 2.3 MB. SEBI issued that circular in June 2025 and reissued it in
# February 2026 renumbering 376 clauses, and comparing the two is the strongest
# thing this product does. Excluding them meant the deployed site held one
# document and the comparison screen said "there is nothing to compare this
# against yet", so the amendment journey could not be shown on the live site at
# all. That was found by testing the deployment rather than the code.
corpus/depositories-*.pdf
corpus/research-analysts-*.pdf
corpus/mutual-funds-*.pdf
corpus/short-*.pdf
